{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "API Consistency Hook",
  "description": "Verifies that DTOs, endpoints and documentation are aligned when API files are modified in the traffic system",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/traffic_system/api/**/*"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "API files have been modified in the traffic system. Please verify that:\n\n1. **DTOs (Data Transfer Objects)** in `src/traffic_system/core/api_models.py` are consistent with the API changes\n2. **API endpoints** in the modified files have matching request/response models\n3. **Documentation** reflects the current API structure and any new endpoints\n4. **Pydantic validation** is properly implemented for all new data models\n5. **Type annotations** are complete and accurate\n6. **Error handling** follows the project standards with proper ValidationError handling\n\nFocus on ensuring consistency between:\n- API endpoint definitions\n- Request/response DTOs in api_models.py\n- Configuration models in config_models.py (if API config changed)\n- Any related documentation\n\nCheck that all changes maintain the microservices architecture patterns and follow the project's type safety requirements."
  }
}
